WEBVTT

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.890
Puzzles are chains...

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.730
Puzzles are mirrors.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.190
Isn’t that right, Jin?

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.480
Oh, sweet! Let’s go, Jin!

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.620
Yeah...

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.240
This is... a puzzle?

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.090
It’s a Philosopher’s Puzzle.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.100
Back when I was a kid, you 
solved it by yourself.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.540
Really? I did that...?

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.540
I guess ya don’t remember, huh?

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.650
There’s a puzzle...

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:23.580
That’s weird.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.790
You already solved this 
back in the day...

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.080
And there are seven balls.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.250
When you solved it, you 
said there were six balls,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.220
making for a total of 720 
total combinations...

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.530
Did someone remake it?

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.720
Whatever! I’ll solve 
any puzzle I come across!

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.080
Please watch, Jin!

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.910
See what I can do now!

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.480
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.020
Raetsel...

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.190
Sorry, my bad!

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.910
It’s not like I’m bored 
being with you, Rook.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:47.600
This is only my second day in 
England, so I’m still jet-lagged!

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.620
Kaito and Jin... Think 
they’re almost done?

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:55.230
Wouldn’t it be nice if 
Jin regained his memories?

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:56.360
Yeah...

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.360
Jin fought with Count Pythagoras...

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.010
and lost his heart to the Puzzle of God.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.410
Fortunately, he has 
regained consciousness.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.880
All that remains are his memories.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.850
Jin, Kaito and I...

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.230
We traveled across this land, 
so even if just a little,

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.140
hopefully this will help 
him remember the past...

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.980
and puzzles.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.340
If he did, I’m sure 
Kaito would be happy.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.980
There are seven slots 
with numbers inside...

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.170
The point of the puzzle is insert the 
colored balls into the correct slots.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.220
There are a total of 5,040 combinations.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.610
The keys leading to 
the correct answer...

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.200
are the balls’ colors 
and the seven numbers.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:49.560
I’ve solved it!

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:53.180
The seven numbers represent 
the number of letters

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.770
for each color in the English alphabet!

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:59.340
In other words, “aka” is 
“red,” which has three letters.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.740
“Ao” is “blue,” 
which has four letters!

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.570
They go...

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.340
here and here!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.280
What’s a Philosopher’s 
Puzzle without a trap?

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.210
But that crap doesn’t scare me!

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:21.280
I’ve got two 5-slots and 
three 6-slots left remaining!

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.480
The structure of the puzzle 
tells me where they go.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.590
It’s a diagram portraying 
the three primary colors.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.010
This is yellow!

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.370
The slots where two circles intersect

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.960
indicate a color created by 
mixing those primary colors!

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.890
Blue and red make purple.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:37.900
It goes in this 6-slot!

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.270
Red and yellow make orange.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.270
It goes in this 6-slot!

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:46.400
Blue and yellow make 
green. It goes here!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:51.740
And in the center, mixing all 
the colors together, you get...

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.580
black in the 5-slot!

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.340
There's no puzzle I can't solve!

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:11.940
Amazing...!

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:14.100
You solved it so quickly...

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:19.000
I can’t believe I was 
absorbed in puzzles.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.310
It’s cool!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.520
I’m sure you’ll remember eventually.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:28.380
And then, the three of us can solve 
puzzles like in the old days...

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.680
Let’s take it slow and easy, Jin.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.540
Kaito...

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:39.400
Oh, yeah! Since I solved 
it, I might as well...

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:43.770
The prize.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.790
Looks like someone remade 
the Philosopher’s Puzzle

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.470
and sealed the prize.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:51.990
It’s a brooch.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.610
Kaito! Jin!

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:09.380
Welcome back, Kaito! Jin!

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.850
Welcome back, Kaito.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:20.000
Nonoha and Rook, welcome 
back after a long day!

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:23.060
We’ll be staying here 
again tonight, Freecell.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.290
Sorry, Freecell!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.620
We’ve been using the 
school dorms like a hotel.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:30.840
I don’t mind. I was 
able to get permission.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.160
So, how’s Jin?

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.050
Tomorrow...

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:42.520
we’ll try taking him to the 
puzzle where we first met him.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.790
Say, would you two care to join us?

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.250
Really? Sounds fun.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.470
Let’s go, Freecell.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.060
Uh, no...

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.840
I no longer play puzzles...

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.030
That right? Okay, then.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.890
Man, I’m starving!

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:00.870
Dinner is ready.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:02.690
Come right this way.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.980
Jin, they said it’s chow time!

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.980
C’mon, Jin!

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:11.720
Meow.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.050
Did you say something?

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:17.140
Meow, meow!

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.260
I see you aren’t eating your meal.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.040
I don’t like the food here.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:23.770
This goes against our contract.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.250
Goodness me!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.700
Even three-star restaurants 
mean nothing to you.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.260
Although I must admit, 
the soup was mediocre.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.180
The soup was good!

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.540
Keeping my contract with you is more 
difficult than ruling a country.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.670
The time has finally come, Raetsel.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.420
Let us pray that each of our 
missions ends in success.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.430
I’m super pissed here!

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:04.960
Nonoha’s spending 
the night with Kaito?!

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:13.230
<i>Suspicious character detected.</i>

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.400
I was a fool to go along 
with it when Kaito

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.020
said he needed a girl to help out!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.670
Not quite, Iwashimizu!

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:14.740
Gammon may be a weirdo, but he’s 
not a “suspicious character.”

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.470
<i>A weirdo.</i>

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:19.030
I, Ana, think you’re 
worrying too much!

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.180
Rook-Rook and Jin-Jin are both with her.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.230
But--But, Mom!

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:24.750
Don’t, “But, Mom!” me.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.370
Besides, I, Ana, am a boy.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:28.960
Nonoha!

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:31.280
Crap!

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:38.540
Please come back in one piece! Nonoha!

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:40.170
<i>Weirdo. Weirdo.</i>

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.170
I see things haven’t changed.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:43.600
Nonoha!

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:42.810
Souji!

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.870
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.000
Guys, long time no see!

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.560
College Souji, you look cool!

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.660
You’ll come back safe 
and sound, won’t you?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.330
Thank you.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.290
Eh?!

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.270
What the hell?

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:09.610
In other words, when Jin 
Makata was a member of POG,

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:13.480
he would do anything to win, 
even changing the rules.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.300
He was a delinquent as a Giver.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:21.180
Yesterday, I was searching the POG’s 
digital library for a college report...

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:24.180
and stumbled on that file.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.710
I don’t believe that report!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:30.310
It doesn’t match the image 
of the guy Kaito paints at all.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.590
I, Ana, think... it’s phooey!

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.740
Right... You’re right!

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.090
I was getting worked up over nothing.

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.940
This is where we first met you, Jin.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:58.740
Yeah! We were lost in this 
maze and you saved us, Jin.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.320
This is my first time coming!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.310
Is this another Philosopher’s Puzzle?

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.440
This is a Puzzle of Fools.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.810
Those unable to solve 
it lose their lives.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:14.780
Their lives...?!

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:21.430
The trap system has been dismantled.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.160
It’s safe now.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:24.710
Let’s go.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:35.040
I betrayed Kaito in 
this Puzzle of Fools.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.960
I hurt Kaito, toyed with our friendship,

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.840
and pushed myself down 
the path of destruction.

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:45.830
Even though I was consumed 
by the Armlet of Orpheus...

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:48.180
Don’t let that weigh 
down on you forever, Rook.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.680
You’re different now!

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.500
Yes, you’re right.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.480
Kaito, Rook...

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:02.910
Didn’t you say that I’m the one 
who taught you how to solve puzzles?

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.910
Puzzles... Are puzzles something 
that we need to have in this world?

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:13.250
What brought that on so suddenly, Jin?

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.270
Let’s head back...

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:16.110
Jin!

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:16.750
Jin!

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.690
Wait, Jin! What’s gotten into--

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.380
Stop! Jin!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.070
Did you sense that, Rook?

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:25.840
Yeah.

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:30.420
This is...

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.960
It feels different than it did earlier.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:38.130
I’m sensing serious malice 
coming from this puzzle!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.710
You can sense that sorta stuff too, huh?

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.800
Fascinating!

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.330
Who’re you?!

00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.150
Jin!

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:02.760
Wh-what are you doing?!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:06.460
I’ve missed you, Jin!

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.020
You know Jin’s name...!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.000
Raetsel...

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:16.900
That’s right. I’m Raetsel, Jin.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.990
Jin remembered her name...

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.600
Do you remember everything now, Jin?

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:34.060
No, just her name...

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:36.160
Who are you?

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:39.000
There were a total 5,040 combinations.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.440
Give it back.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:44.010
That was mine.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:47.630
Are you the one who remade 
the Philosopher’s Puzzle

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.750
we visited yesterday?

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:52.890
Thank you, Jin.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.640
Who the heck are you?!

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:56.640
You!

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.150
You don’t know anything, 
do you? About Jin...

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.760
What Jin needs...

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:08.680
is me!

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:09.820
Hey!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:12.900
Wait!

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:20.630
Kaito Daimon!

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:23.960
You’re a nuisance, punk!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:27.130
It’s blinding!

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:30.640
She vanished!

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.750
No way! Crap, is this for real?!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.670
Run for it, Rook! Nonoha!

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:41.230
W-wait for me!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:42.840
Turn right, Kaito!

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:43.740
Rook!

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.950
Did she activate it?

00:14:54.930 --> 00:15:09.560
<i>Suspicious character detected.
Suspicious character detected.</i>

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.400
Who’re you?! Need somethin’?

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.780
I am Enigma.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:12.120
I am the one who leads the Master Brain.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.350
Master Brain?

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:17.980
They are a group of genius givers 
who hunt Phi-Brain children.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.690
What is that?!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:25.850
It’s a puzzle!

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.160
It’s a little present.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:33.320
If you don’t solve the puzzle within 
the time limit, he’ll go, “Kaboom!”

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:38.000
No way! Hey, Gammon! Hurry and solve it!

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.560
Wh-what’s with this situation?!

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:43.330
Sheeit! It’s an annoying 
game with numbers!

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.330
What is the meaning of this?!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.300
What are you after?!

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:48.710
The annihilation of all puzzlers...

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.460
in accordance with a pledge 
I swore to Jin Makata.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.890
The annihilation of all puzzlers?!

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:55.700
That doesn’t make sense!

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:58.890
And why is Jin Makata’s name 
poppin’ up in all of this?!

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:02.560
“Challenge the puzzlers who 
endanger the world with puzzles.”

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.390
“Make them taste the 
ultimate humiliation

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:08.900
through their defeat and 
then destroy them.”

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:12.050
“Do whatever it takes to win.”

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.030
Those were Jin’s thoughts.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.260
You can do it, Gammon! Hurry! Hurry!

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:19.770
Hence I’ve decided to start by 
eliminating the Phi-Brain children,

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:21.980
for you are the figureheads 
of all puzzlers.

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.090
“Do whatever it takes to win.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:27.420
That matches what Upperclassman 
Jikukawa said earlier.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.670
That’s absurd!

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:31.140
You don’t seem to believe me.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.640
Then why don’t you see what has

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:36.300
become of your friends who are

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.160
currently with Jin?

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:42.310
Iwashimizu, emergency search for Kaito!

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:43.620
<i>Roger!</i>

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:47.510
Left, Kaito!

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.110
Which way should I go next?

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.590
His thought process is accelerating!

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.830
Kaito is currently risking his 
life to solve a Puzzle of Fools!

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:58.810
What?!

00:16:58.810 --> 00:16:59.790
F-for real...?

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:05.600
We will destroy the Phi-Brain 
children with puzzles.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.270
It would seem Jin Makata’s 
dream is becoming a reality.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.450
That is ridiculous nonsense.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:15.600
I would like you to stop 
telling my students

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.350
false stories that 
lack a shred of truth,

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:22.220
President Johan Sigmund Enigma.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.210
What?!

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:24.100
Pre--?!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.870
President?!

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:30.050
Most impressive, Baron Kaidou.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.170
I see you keep up with 
your foreign politics.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.990
But Jin Makata’s blank year.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.370
Even you, his best friend, don’t 
know what that year means.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:39.490
Shut up!

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.060
Principal...?

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.270
Got it! Solved!

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:48.130
What?! The countdown ain’t stoppin’!

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.640
You were messin’ with us!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.960
Well, I shall be taking my leave now.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.110
Whodunit!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.650
The rest is in your hands.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:15.300
Bastard! Get back here!

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.430
Wanted men!

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:21.530
You get to face me!

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:27.140
If you can’t solve my puzzle, just 
like you’re buddies, you’re...!

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:37.150
Nonoha, stop them! Go stop those things!

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:38.160
Huh?

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:40.630
With your brute strength, 
you can do it! Go for it!

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:42.370
Keep dreaming!

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.180
It was unpleasant, wasn’t it?

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.560
The way she talked.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.160
What?

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.450
This maze has been tweaked so that

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.800
none of the paths will 
take us to the entrance.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.650
No way! Then what’ll we do?!

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.650
This maze has another exit.

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:59.660
We should be able to dodge 
the traps and get there!

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.510
Are you sure there’s an exit, Rook?

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:06.250
Once, I searched this maze over 
so that I could ensnare you.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:07.980
This way!

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.250
That’s it!

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.560
Hurry! Nonoha! Kaito!

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.170
That had me in for a scare!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:39.260
You were a lifesaver, Rook!

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.850
Wh-what is that?

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:49.690
This room...

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:50.900
It’s different!

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:54.250
When I came last, there 
were only two doors.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:55.420
What?!

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.070
There are a total of twelve doors, huh?

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:01.260
Kaito!

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:03.670
Let’s hurry out of here.

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:06.160
The exit is the door 
opposite of the entrance.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:09.180
H-hey, wait!

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:23.820
The statue turned?!

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:29.660
Look out, Rook!

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.290
Kaito, up there!

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.260
You’ll die if you open the wrong door.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:48.640
Raetsel!

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:55.770
Jin!

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:57.520
Kaito...

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:04.410
This is a puzzle.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:08.280
Out of the 12 doors, find the 
one leading to the outside.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:09.910
It’s a puzzle?!

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:17.840
If you open the wrong door, boulders 
will rain on you like just a second ago.

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:20.020
Get it wrong two more times,

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:22.290
and the whole ceiling 
goes “Kersplat!”

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.530
I won’t give any hints!

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:28.280
Kaito, this puzzle is...

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:32.930
Yeah. Without any clues, 
it’s super hard!

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:39.940
I hate slowpokes!

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:42.300
Hurry and solve it!

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:43.070
Raetsel!

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.800
Who the heck are you?!

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.720
Why are you doing this?!

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:49.970
Why?

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:53.230
I’m going to defeat you with a puzzle.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:56.620
I’m using the thing Jin hated 
and detested above all else,

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:00.090
wishing that they’d fall of 
the face of the planet: Puzzles!

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:03.090
Jin?! Hates puzzles?!

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:07.340
Puzzles... Are puzzles something 
that we need to have in this world?

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:09.530
Jin hates puzzles...?

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.100
He detested them?

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:17.830
Jin, watch as Kaito Daimon loses 
pathetically before your very eyes.

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:20.770
Raetsel...

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:05.360
Kaito’s in a pinch?!

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:07.570
Which means starting next week, 
the protagonist will be...

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:09.760
<i>I am Kaito Daimon.</i>

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:12.550
You’re Iwashimizu! 
What’re you doing here?!

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:15.030
<i>I’ll solve all of the puzzles!</i>

00:24:15.030 --> 00:24:17.620
Get off yer high horse! Dang, 
he’s blowing me off...

00:24:17.770 --> 00:24:20.270
<i>Next time: You Don’t Know Anything</i>

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:27.970
You Don’t Know Anything

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:22.250
<i>There is no puzzle I can't solve!</i>

00:24:22.250 --> 00:24:24.190
There is no puzzle you CAN solve!
